positions.six_steps:
The six steps, one line each: (1) create the map and the rules; (2) stress-test the rules; (3) translate everything; (4) compile; (5) run it; (6) match behavior. Here is what each means in this repo.

Pre-Step 1, build the judge (prompts/00b-judge-setup.md). There are about 9 harness tasks: commit the --nodaemon fix and run the 272 cases 3 times; add the parity mode; the restart script; the --ps-protocol diff; the bindings socket-path fix with a macOS build and the async exec_* tests; one wasm command; sysbench plus start-up timing; the coverage run; and the expression/cast corpus. They cover 13 scenario families. Validation is on C++ HEAD and on mutated C++.

Step 1, create the map and the rules (prompts/01-dependency-map.md, prompts/02-gap-inventory.md). Because this is a redesign, the rulebook is a design document built on templates/RULEBOOK.md. It fixes:
- the crate graph: 20-40 crates seeded from bazel/architecture/module_policy.bzl and the Bazel group targets (src/sql/sql_runtime_group_deps.bzl);
- the error type generated from ob_errno.def;
- the arena and handoff rules;
- the IR ids;
- the column batch;
- the storage filter trait;
- the context struct;
- the OOM policy;
- the unsafe policy;
- the island ABIs;
- the wasm rules: u64 for persisted and wire fields, no 128-bit atomics, bounded recursion, networking behind cargo features.
The map: adapt scripts/depmap_c.py to include edges plus a pass that finds where each class is defined, because 53 forwarder/.cpp pairs cross groups. Condense to the proposed crates. Today the include graph has one cycle of 110 directories, and 4 top-level violating lines from d51422b54. The manifest comes from scripts/make_manifest.py.
The inventory holds only the sites the design rules do not decide:
- about 823 ATOMIC_* field names;
- 441 inc_ref/dec_ref lines and 130 Handle classes;
- 1,733 const_cast lines;
- 4,189 comparisons of error codes;
- 1,560 tmp_ret/OB_TMP_FAIL lines;
- 31 comparators that carry an error code;
- about 40 budget-backed OOM sites plus the logical -4013 errors;
- the 122 server_service slot types;
- the base classes that upper code subclasses.

Step 2, stress-test the rules (prompts/03-stress-test.md). For the core the bakeoff is invalid (README). Use adversarial review of the design doc plus disposable full runs of one narrow end-to-end path, thrown away after measuring. For the leaves, run 03 as written against the frozen core API, on 3 stems scored by risk. For example: a slice of ob_transform_utils.cpp (pointer identity), an expression that reads the session and uses casts, and a slice of ob_join_order.cpp (cost floats).

Between Steps 2 and 3, build the core. This is hand work and not a kit step. It covers about 300K C++ lines, measured:
- 57,762 in the oblib substrate directories;
- 17,744 in datum, object and rc;
- 42,825 in the IR;
- 43,808 in the execution framework and code generator;
- 137,103 in tablet, meta_mem, memtable, tx, multi_data_source, tx_table and data_plane access.
The gate is the judge's growing plain-SQL subset.

Step 3, translate everything (prompts/04-translation-kickoff.md, scripts/queue_runner.mjs). The units are the leaf stems: 3,692 hand-written stems, minus about 480 in the core (an assumption, proportional to lines), minus 113 share/geo stems kept in C++, which leaves about 3,100. Splitting the 54 files of 4K lines or more gives about 3,000-4,000 units. Each unit gets its stem (median 2.6K tokens), a generated declaration index in place of raw headers (one-level context median 25.6K tokens; full closure median 1.4-2.4M), the design doc and its inventory rows. The order is the crate graph.

Step 4, compile (prompts/05-survey-build.md, scripts/build_daemon.sh). One cargo check survey per crate, leaves to root. Fold into Step 3 only if the Phase 1 pilot shows at most about 60 s per crate. templates/settings.json denies are installed by the developer before 03.

Step 5, run it (no prompt). Hello world means: the Rust binary bootstraps an empty base dir, sql-nio answers `select 1`, and tools/deploy/init.sql and init_user.sql run with zero errors. Smoke means: the 130 plain-SQL cases, then the bindings and async suites.

Step 6, match behavior (the 00b judge, then prompts/06-post-parity.md after the gate). Burn down the 272 cases and the 13 scenario families. Triage each failure by running it on C++ (inherited, regression or environment). The done-gate: every parity scenario passes, and C++ re-runs clean. Then 06 works through the BUG(port), TODO(port) and PERF(port) markers.

Cutover: bump the data version, move the gate ahead of the meta.db open (ob_server.cpp:1698-1719), and close the missing-file hole (ob_data_version_mgr.cpp:88-94).

risks:
The target keeps moving:
- upstream changes by about 8K lines a month;
- feature/plugin adds +105,879 code lines, 34.6K of them Rust;
- feat/embedded-mode is 197 commits ahead;
- the wasm branch touches 366 files;
- 18 open 'Remove ...' issues.

Hazards if any Rust piece is linked into the C++ binary during the transition, for example for testing:
- only one Rust staticlib can be linked (duplicate std);
- freeing memory across the languages depends on the shared jemalloc, through the malloc hook on Linux and zone promotion on macOS;
- clang 17 and rustc's LLVM 22 differ, so there is no cross-language LTO.

